<https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes> a dcat:Dataset;
  dcterms:title "Linked.Archi Architecture Processes Extension"@en;
  dcterms:description """Extension ontology describing architecture governance processes,
activities, tasks, and their inputs and outputs.

Architecture processes are not constituents of the system being architected —
they are the governance and lifecycle infrastructure that acts upon it from the
outside. An architecture review board process governs a system; it is not part
of the system's architecture. They are elements of a model all the same — of a
model of the architecture practice: a process, its activities, tasks,
deliverables and milestones are element types (arch:Element), so that a
modelling tool can place them in a view beside the architecture they govern.
Process concepts relate to the elements of that architecture via linking
properties (ap:governs, ap:input, ap:output, ap:consumedBy), never by being
one of its components.

Use this extension when you need to:
* Describe architecture governance processes and their decomposition
* Capture process inputs (forces, models, information items) and outputs
  (decisions, deliverables, models)
* Trace how architecture activities relate to decisions and deliverables
* Link architecture elements to the processes that govern them

The process concepts are aligned with ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020 (architecture governance),
ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 (software lifecycle), and ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 (system lifecycle).
For the normative standard definitions themselves, see the corresponding standard
vocabularies under standards/."""@en;
  dcterms:conformsTo owl:Ontology;
  vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes#";
  vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "ap";
  owl:versionInfo "0.4.0";
  dcterms:modified "2026-11-17"^^xsd:date;
  adms:status <http://purl.org/adms/status/UnderDevelopment>;
  dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
  dcterms:creator [ a foaf:Person;
      foaf:name "Kalin Maldzhanski"
    ];
  dcat:theme <https://meta.linked.archi/catalog#extensions>;
  dcat:landingPage <https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes/>;
  dcat:distribution [ a dcat:Distribution;
