<https://meta.linked.archi/archimate3/relationship-tables> a dcat:Dataset;
  dcterms:title "Linked.Archi ArchiMate 3.2 Relationship Tables"@en;
  dcterms:description """The relationship tables of ArchiMate 3.2 (Appendix B.5) as lookups: for
each element type, the types each relationship may go to — directly, or as the result of a
derivation — as annotations on the element type (am:Artifact :permitsRealization am:BusinessObject),
and for each relationship the annotation that holds its permissions (am:realizes :permittedBy
:permitsRealization). A relationship permitted to every element type lists arch:Element, and to
every element and relationship arch:ModelConcept.

Each permission also says whether it is direct: :permitsDirectRealization, a subproperty of
:permitsRealization (am:realizes :permittedDirectlyBy :permitsDirectRealization), lists the types the
tables print in upper case — a relationship a modeller may draw. A type :permits… but not
:permitsDirect… is one the specification sanctions only as the conclusion of a derivation. The
relationships to and from relationships, which Table 21 lists without case, are direct, as
association is in the tables, and a grouping's aggregation and composition.

The same tables as the relationship shapes (archimate3.2-relationship-shapes.ttl), generated from the
same matrix, in a form for another use. The shapes validate: SHACL Core, which any SHACL engine runs
and which reports a relationship the tables forbid. These answer a lookup — may this relationship go
from this type to that one, and may a modeller draw it? — with one triple pattern. A tool may use
either: the shapes to validate, and to read the table back out of their sh:or lists; these to look a
relationship up, and to tell one a modeller may draw from one only a derivation gives.

The derivation rules (archimate3.2-derivation-rules.ttl) use these: a SHACL rule queries the data
graph, where the shapes are not, and reading the shapes' lists in SPARQL is slow. A potential rule
derives only what these permit from the one element type to the other, so load this file with the
model to run them: without it, the potential rules derive nothing.

Each relationship the specification's metamodel figures draw is given too: :drawsRealization, a
subproperty of :permitsRealization (am:realizes :drawnBy :drawsRealization), lists the types the figures
draw a realization to from this type — expanded from the abstract types a figure names to the concrete
pairs beneath them that the tables permit directly. They say what the specification illustrates, which a
modelling tool may show; the order in which it proposes relationships is the taxonomy's. Each such
triple's reifier cites, with dcterms:source, every figure that draws it. The generic figures hold within
a layer: across layers the tables give their triggering, flow, access and assignment only as derived (a
business process accessing a data object), and the figures of Chapter 12 draw what holds between layers.
They leave the implementation and migration elements out too, which 3.2 classifies as internal
behaviour, event and passive structure elements: their own figures draw their relationships. A pair a
figure names itself is given as the figure draws it: figure 113 draws a work package realizing and
influencing a requirement, which the tables give only as derived.

This is not an official Open Group document."""@en;
  dcterms:conformsTo owl:Ontology;
  vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://meta.linked.archi/archimate3/relationship-tables#";
  vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "amrt";
  owl:versionInfo "3.2";
  dcterms:modified "2026-10-16"^^xsd:date;
  adms:status <http://purl.org/adms/status/UnderDevelopment>;
  dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
  dcterms:creator [ a foaf:Person;
      foaf:name "Kalin Maldzhanski"
    ];
  dcat:theme <https://meta.linked.archi/catalog#languages>;
  dcat:keyword "ArchiMate 3.2"@en;
  dcat:landingPage <https://meta.linked.archi/archimate3/relationship-tables/>;
  dcat:distribution [ a dcat:Distribution;
      dcat:accessURL <https://meta.linked.archi/archimate3/relationship-tables/archimate3.2-relationship-tables.ttl>;
      dcat:downloadURL <https://meta.linked.archi/archimate3/relationship-tables/archimate3.2-relationship-tables.ttl>;
      dcat:mediaType <http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/turtle>
    ] .

