<https://meta.linked.archi/archimate4/viewpoint-shapes> a dcat:Dataset;
  dcterms:title "Linked.Archi ArchiMate 4.0 Viewpoint Conformance Shapes"@en;
  dcterms:description """Viewpoint conformance for ArchiMate 4.0 models. The rules are in the core
shapes, which this document imports, and it adds none of its own:

1. Viewpoint declaration — every View declares exactly one viewpoint, as an
   arch:Viewpoint individual rather than a literal.
2. View type conformance — a View's rdf:type must match one of the viewpoint's
   arch:viewType values (Diagram, Catalog, Matrix).
3. Element conformance — elements presented in a View, linked by arch:inView,
   must be instances of types the viewpoint's arch:includesConcept allows.
4. Relationship endpoint conformance — the endpoints of a relationship drawn on
   a View should themselves be in the viewpoint's palette.
5. Viewpoint completeness — a viewpoint should declare what it admits, the
   concerns it frames and which kinds of view realise it.

They read the viewpoint definitions from the loaded graph rather than naming any
viewpoint, and use no ArchiMate term, so core states them once for every language:
the published 4.0 catalogue, custom viewpoints and other frameworks' alike. A rule
that only ArchiMate 4.0 viewpoints need would go here.

Usage: load the core shapes with the 4.0 viewpoint catalogue and the model.
core-onto.ttl and the 4.0 ontology go in the shapes graph and the data: the shapes
target arch:View and arch:Viewpoint, and their SPARQL walks rdfs:subClassOf* in
the data."""@en;
  dcterms:conformsTo owl:Ontology;
  vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://meta.linked.archi/archimate4/viewpoint-shapes#";
  vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "am4vpsh";
  owl:versionInfo "4.0";
  dcterms:modified "2026-11-06"^^xsd:date;
  adms:status <http://purl.org/adms/status/UnderDevelopment>;
  dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
  dcterms:creator [ a foaf:Person;
